.SH NAME
maknoon-reassemble - Reconstruct a file from fragments


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmaknoon reassemble [dir] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Reconstructs the original file from a directory of .maknf shard files.
Requires at least N data shards (as specified during fragmentation).

.PP
Use --verify to check the output SHA-256 against the hash stored in manifest.json,
confirming the reconstruction is byte-perfect:

.PP
maknoon reassemble /tmp/recover/ --output secret.makn --verify


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--authorized-key\fP=""
	ML-DSA public key to verify shard integrity

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for reassemble

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=""
	Path to save the reconstructed file

.PP
\fB--verify\fP[=false]
	Verify output SHA-256 against manifest.json (recommended)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--fips\fP[=false]
	Enforce strict FIPS-140 compliant cryptographic standards

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Output results in JSON format

.PP
\fB--policy\fP=""
	Path to a declarative governance policy file (JSON)

.PP
\fB--tpm\fP[=false]
	Enable TPM 2.0 hardware-backed storage for keys

.PP
